107
00:06:31,923 --> 00:06:34,269
Rym: I'm actually really bad at jumping for all the other stuff I'm good at.

108
00:06:35,230 --> 00:06:41,266
Scott: I remember at Lake Placid, you could see the ski jumps from the Olympics and they're old and sad and no one uses those.

109
00:06:43,511 --> 00:06:47,696
Rym: But the way those work, those you do just go straight down.

110
00:06:47,977 --> 00:06:52,582
Rym: They kind of just lock you in like your two skis are almost like side rails.

111
00:06:52,782 --> 00:06:58,930
Rym: They just hold you straight because the only thing you're being judged on is your form once you hit the jump.

112
00:06:59,530 --> 00:07:01,534
Rym: So the slope is not normal skiing.

113
00:07:01,614 --> 00:07:09,328
Rym: It's just a mechanism to make sure everybody jumps at the exact same point the exact same way and then they judge you on how well you do it after you take off.

114
00:07:12,832 --> 00:07:18,446
Scott: You could see the Lake Placid Olympic jumping complex on Google Maps.

115
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:22,036
Rym: I hiked past it once.

116
00:07:22,056 --> 00:07:24,128
Rym: That was a long time ago.

117
